summary: |-
  Restart anchor for the Warpline arc. Warpline (packages/warpline/) is git's REPLACEMENT — a meaning-primary VCS — coexisting with git for this project while it accumulates its own history. This multi-session run built the entire WRITE PATH: single-writer history (pick/fabric/strand/seal + auto-seal hook), the false-AUTOFOLD safety gate, multi-writer admission (scratch/admit: FAST_ADMIT/CLEAN/KNOT/DANGLE), meaning→bytes materialization (merge3/materialize — performs merges git conflicts on), the KNOT council (resolve), the calibration moat (grade — confidence vs real outcome), cross-process concurrency safety (fabric-lock + selvage CAS), and fail-closed hardening (binary/large-file/3rd-gen-merge). A team audit redirected away from per-domain CAS toward this hardening + the moat. 173 tests green; HEAD a7acfac1 on branch warpline-surfaces (pushed); fabric has 10 real strands of this project's own history.</summary>
