body: |-
  ORIENTATION (read this first on restart):
  - Warpline = meaning-primary VCS, git REPLACEMENT (NOT a pivot/companion — that was a misread; replacement was the goal from the arc's start). Coexists with git for a-paradigm now (we keep pushing git) while accumulating its OWN meaning-history under .warpline/. Engine: packages/warpline/. Spec/symbol map: packages/warpline/.purpose.
  - Branch warpline-surfaces, HEAD a7acfac1 (pushed to origin). 173 tests green. The .warpline/fabric.jsonl ledger (tracked) + refs/selvage are the project's native history (10 strands); states/ + grades.jsonl + oracle.jsonl are gitignored (regenerable).

  THE WRITE-PATH STACK (all built this run, src/fabric/):
  - #strand/#fabric/#seal — a sealed PICK is a strand; #seal is the SINGLE fabric writer (pick/admit/resolve all route through it); stateId=reproducible meaning address, pickId=event identity (EXCLUDES calibratedConfidence so grading can mutate it).
  - #pick + #hook — `warpline pick` seals working meaning; the post-commit auto-seal hook accrues a strand on every git commit (recorded BOTH agents' commits when a classroom agent ran concurrently). `warpline log`/`selvage`.
  - #scratch/#admit (multi-writer DECISION) — fork a per-agent base, admit → FAST_ADMIT / CLEAN (gate-rule confidence linked|independent) / KNOT / DANGLE.
  - #merge3/#materialize (meaning→bytes) — token-level 3-way merge PERFORMS the merge git's line-merge conflicts on; admit materializes + seals on CLEAN; byte-faithful.
  - #resolve (KNOT council) — human resolution sealed with a `resolves` envelope (decidedBy/reason/contended) — accountability git's merge commit can't keep.
  - #grade (the MOAT) — seeds confidence from the gate rule, grades it against real survive/overturn outcome (classroom certify→outcome model). Backfilled live (80% pick survival). `warpline grade`.
  - #fabric-lock + selvage CAS — cross-process O_EXCL lock + check-then-append-then-publish, closing the lost-update race (the hook backgrounds its seal).
  - HARDENING (fail-closed, never corrupt): H3 binary→conflict, M1 oversized→conflict, H1 3rd-gen-merge-onto-a-merge-strand→unsealed (merge strands marked strand.merged).

  KEY FINDING — the false-AUTOFOLD gate (T-013, the SHIP-GATE): the engine catches a cross-symbol semantic conflict IFF a dependency path links the symbols in-graph (Merkle-by-target propagation). Dependency-LINKED → caught; INDEPENDENT / cross-file → BLIND (silent false-CLEAN). The SAME double-tax bug is caught same-file, blind cross-file. This is WHY admit's CLEAN confidence defaults to 'independent'=hedged 0.6, and why a primary auto-admitting store must surface/confirm rather than silently merge.

  THE AUDIT (TD-2026-06-27-798) — team (Arky/Rune/Reviewer/Loid) converged: DEFER per-domain CAS (premature for 2-5 agents + was built on an unsynchronized selvage — the real gap, now fixed). Calibration > CAS (the only thing git can't replicate). Multi-writer not dogfood-ready until the hardening (now mostly done). Per-domain CAS granularity design captured for if/when needed (owning-dir of authored stableKeys, bounded by empty-delta ripple).

  OPEN TASKS (restart from these): T-2026-06-27-002 remaining hardening (H2 rename -M, mode-change detection, G-tests: interleaved 3+ agents / KNOT-downgrade / multi-file) — last dogfood-blocker; T-2026-06-27-004 author the Warpline University course in the ai-literacy pack (dogfoods University; moat is live now so it can teach a real graded field); T-2026-06-27-001 FRAMEWORK BUG ~~read-only (rebuild paradigm-mcp dist — the f6008cf2 fix never compiled); T-2026-06-27-005 symbol hygiene (#seal collides with university/ui's seal view; add ~accountability aspect). Loid's dogfood sequence: (d) grade ✓ DONE → (a) course → (c) live two-writer collision capstone (now safe-ish — multi-writer fails closed on the corruption cases).

  KEY LINEAGE: gate L-2026-06-25-ascend-081205-001; pivot/write-path L-2026-06-25-ascend-075114-001; v2 materialize L-2026-06-26-ascend-053504-001; grader+hardening L-2026-06-27-ascend-054450-001; decisions TD-2026-06-25-564 (coexistence) + TD-2026-06-27-798 (defer CAS).</parameter>
